WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.465 --> 00:00:07.360
Speaker 1: Let's let's speak next to Zack&nbsp;
from Toronto, Canada. Zack, you're on the air.&nbsp;

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.160
Speaker 3: Hey, David, can you hear me?
Speaker 1: Yes, I can.&nbsp;

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:20.480
Speaker 3: I was I was curious because I&nbsp;
saw a video on you talking about socialism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:28.240
I was curious of your reasoning of why you&nbsp;
think the means of production should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:34.960
privately owned rather than publicly owned.
Speaker 1: Well, so I approach it a different way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:46.480
And my approach would be why would the means of&nbsp;
production, which might be built by an individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.760
paid for by an individual&nbsp;
insured by an individual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:01:04.000
financed by an individual, why should ownership&nbsp;
be taken away and either made societal or in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.600
communistic sense, state owned? Why why would&nbsp;
we do that? What would be the justification from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:16.240
taking it away from the individual that built it?
Speaker 3:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:22.560
Huh? OK, I am I guess I never thought&nbsp;
about it from like the lottery perspective.&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.200
Speaker 1: Well, I mean, apply it to anything,&nbsp;
right? So so you're sort of like for me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:36.480
the action that would be required to be justified&nbsp;
would be why would why would we be allowed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.120
change the ownership structure of someone?&nbsp;
That's something that someone built. If you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:47.440
you know, you go to school and you learn&nbsp;
plumbing, for example, and then you go and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.880
buy all the plumbing equipment, you might take&nbsp;
out a loan to buy that plumbing equipment. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.640
you're a plumber for a bunch of time. And then&nbsp;
at a certain point, you get big enough where you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.960
start hiring apprentice plumbers and all these&nbsp;
different things. So it's your business. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.680
own the equipment, you hire the employees. What&nbsp;
would be the justification for saying, OK, now the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.880
business is no longer yours, now it belongs to all&nbsp;
of your employees or it belongs to the state. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.560
would be the justification for that?
Speaker 3: Um.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:26.000
I am not sure, actually, I I'm personally&nbsp;
not a socialist, but I'm interested in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:34.240
Socialist theory, and I was just I was curious&nbsp;
of why you personally weren't a socialist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:40.080
but I mean that yeah, that does make sense.
Speaker 1: So I have a ton more broadly. I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:45.440
a ton of videos about why I'm not a socialist. But&nbsp;
to answer that specific question, it's because I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:51.520
don't think there's any justification for it.
Speaker 3: OK, great, thanks, David. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.120
appreciate hearing your perspective.
Speaker 1: I appreciate the question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.560
Thank you so much for calling in.

